--split-spike opens a second, plain window (Vulkan, OpenGL fallback)
pointed at the monitor after the main one's, presenting the bottom
screen alone from the same frames the main presenter drew. its events
only resize and close it, its keyboard never reaches the game, and its
presentation failing closes it and the main window carries on.

the split stays off: not --split-spike, the whole of the window model
is F6 byte-for-byte. comes with the settings' menu and the monitor my
picking, for F7-2 and further.
---
 crates/zakuro/src/cli.rs |   8 ++++
 crates/zakuro/src/lib.rs | 100 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

